Learn how to apply deep learning and neural networks to complex biological and genomic datasets, with applications highly relevant to molecular ecology, microbial ecology, environmental genomics, population ecology, conservation genetics, and evolutionary ecology.

Modern ecological research increasingly generates large and high-dimensional datasets, from environmental DNA and metagenomics to population genomics and microbiome data. Deep learning provides powerful tools for detecting complex biological patterns, classifying genomic sequences, reducing dimensionality, identifying functional genomic elements, and extracting information from datasets that can be difficult to analyse using conventional approaches.

