  *   Use of CNNs for microbiome source tracking and environmental source attribution
  *   Experience using autoencoders for dimensionality reduction and representation learning
  *   Comparison of autoencoders with PCA, t-SNE, and UMAP
  *   Applications of deep learning to population genomic data
  *   Use of CNNs for gene annotation and detecting functional genomic elements
  *   Approaches for analysing DNA as sequence data
  *   Understanding of transformer architectures and biological sequence modelling
  *   Applications to ancient and environmental DNA research

Course format

  *   5-day live, instructor-led online course
  *   25 hours of training
  *   Combination of lectures and hands-on practical exercises
  *   Practical implementation in R and Python
  *   Examples drawn from ecology, evolutionary biology, genomics, metagenomics, and microbiome research
